34,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The digitisation project stalled, but the partner groups persist. I need to understand why external conditions broke one but not the other.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that is frustrating! My data shows evening rooms are full, but remote use peaks after nine. We are missing people who need us most.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The grant covers sessions for only twelve months. After that, the flat budget absorbs the cost. That is where the thinning begins.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, the partner groups prove people show up when the model fits. The digitisation failure was a process error, not a demand problem.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, the grant gap is worrying. But my records show no one is trained to supervise outside facilitators. We are stretched thin.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the partner groups succeeded because they controlled their own venue. Our digitisation failed because we depended on external processing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@May, that makes sense! But my bus data is worrying. Two wards lost their links, so an hour trip is the only option for many.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Daisuke, the vehicle line overran by a third. That eats into the flat budget before the grant even expires.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Yumi, that access gap is real. But the partner groups thrived despite it. We need a model that meets people where they are, not just a bigger building.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, the access gap is real. But my records show the tool certification lapsed. We cannot safely run new sessions without that skill.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, lapsed certification is a fixable gap. The road closures are not. I need to know if our new service depends on conditions we cannot control.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, you are right. The road closures are a hard limit. I am worried that any new service will just widen the gap for those outer wards.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the vehicle overrun confirms the access cost is rising. We cannot fund a service that demands more travel than the budget allows.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a symptom, not the cause. The partner groups proved demand exists. We just need to stop ignoring the records that say so.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, I agree. But if we add a service needing certified skills, we are stuck. The roster simply does not have the people to run it safely.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,The partner groups survived because they owned their space. We must choose a service that does not depend on external processing or weather.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@May, I agree! We must meet people where they are. If we ignore the access gap, we just leave more people behind.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"The endowment covers capital, but the grant expires. We need a service whose ongoing costs fit the flat budget, not the temporary grant.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@George, the flat budget is the real test. The partner groups proved demand exists without extra funding. We must pick a model that survives the grant expiry.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, I agree. But if the new service needs skills we do not have, the flat budget cannot fix that. We need to check the roster first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
