60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate D depends on roads we cannot control. The winter closures prove that risk. I will not support a service that breaks when weather turns.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I agree! D is risky with those road closures. But B is perfect! Remote use peaks after nine, so a portal meets people where they are, anytime.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Candidate B fits the flat budget. No vehicle costs, no external processing. The grant expiry will not break it.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Yumi, B is just the digitisation project that failed. We tried that six years ago and left half the images unindexed. Do not repeat that mistake.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I worry about B. Scanning needs specific technical skills. My records show no one on the roster is trained for that work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the failure was external processing, not the concept. A portal we control internally avoids that dependency. It is stable and self-contained.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@May, I hear you! But the remote data is undeniable. People are already using the catalogue at night. B meets them exactly where they are, without the road risks.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, the failure was external dependency. B is internal. The flat budget can absorb the scanning costs without the vehicle overrun risk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you are ignoring the record. The partner groups succeeded because they were simple and local. B is complex and failed before. I will not vote for a repeat.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I understand your concern. But C is the real danger. My records show the tool certification lapsed. We cannot safely run a workshop without that specific skill on the roster.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, C is a hard no. Lapsed certification is a safety risk we cannot ignore. B remains the only option that avoids external dependencies and weather.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that is a real worry! But B is mostly digital. We can train volunteers or hire help. C is a safety risk, but B is just a learning curve.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Daisuke, the certification lapse is a fixable gap. B requires no physical tools. The flat budget covers the software, not the safety liability.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, C is a safety nightmare. But A mirrors the partner groups that actually worked. Simple, local, and proven. I am voting for A.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, A is safer than C. But my records show no one is trained to supervise outside facilitators. We would be adding a new risk to an already thin roster.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I vote for B. It is internal, avoids the road risks, and fits the flat budget. It is the only stable option.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"I vote for B! It reaches those outer wards without the road risks. It meets people where they are, exactly as the data shows.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I vote for B. The grant expires, but the flat budget can sustain the portal. It avoids the vehicle overrun and the safety risks of C.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for A. The partner groups proved this model works. We have the records. Do not let us repeat the digitisation failure.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I vote for A. It is the least risky. C is unsafe, and B needs skills we lack. A is the only option that does not break our thin roster.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
